---
import ProjectLayout from "../../../layouts/ProjectLayout.astro";
import ProjectFacts from "../../../components/projects/ProjectFacts.astro";
import ProjectFact from "../../../components/projects/ProjectFact.astro";

// Plain ASCII on purpose: box-drawing glyphs aren't in the font's latin
// subset and would fall back to another font, breaking the alignment.
const diagram = ` exchanges  registrars    gmp
 & filings  & brokers   trackers
     |          |          |
     +----------+----------+
                |
   +------------v------------+
   |        ipoalerts        |
   |   merges, cleans and    |
   |   refreshes every ipo   |
   +-------------------------+
   | GET /ipos               |
   | GET /ipos/{id}/gmp      |
   +------------+------------+
                |
     fintech apps & websites`;

// A real response from October 2026, trimmed to the interesting fields.
const sample = `$ curl "https://api.ipoalerts.in/ipos?status=open" \\
    -H "x-api-key: YOUR_API_KEY"

{
  "ipos": [
    {
      "name": "HD Fire Protect Limited",
      "symbol": "HDFIRE",
      "status": "open",
      "startDate": "2026-10-13",
      "endDate": "2026-10-15",
      "listingDate": "2026-10-21",
      "priceRange": "258-271",
      "minQty": 55,
      "minAmount": 14905,
      "issueSize": "712cr",
      "subscription": { "timesSubscribed": 10.99 },
      ...
    }
  ]
}`;
---

<ProjectLayout project="ipoalerts">
	<section class="intro">
		<p>
			ipoalerts is an API for IPO data in India. Fintech apps and websites
			plug into it to show which IPOs are open, what's coming up, how heavily
			an issue is subscribed and where its grey market premium is heading,
			without scraping a dozen sources themselves.
		</p>
		<p>
			It started in 2021 as a weekend project that emailed people about IPOs.
			It's been an API since 2024, and these days it powers 500+ apps and
			websites.
		</p>
	</section>

	<ProjectFacts>
		<ProjectFact label="what">IPO and GMP data APIs for Indian markets</ProjectFact>
		<ProjectFact label="covers">
			Mainboard, SME and debt issues on NSE & BSE, back to 2012
		</ProjectFact>
		<ProjectFact label="started">a weekend project, in April 2021</ProjectFact>
		<ProjectFact label="used by">500+ apps and websites</ProjectFact>
		<ProjectFact label="pricing">
			free tier; <a href="https://ipoalerts.in/pricing" data-umami-event="ipoalerts-pricing">paid plans</a> from ₹499 a month
		</ProjectFact>
		<ProjectFact label="status">live</ProjectFact>
	</ProjectFacts>

	<h2>How it started</h2>

	<p>
		India had an IPO boom in early 2021, and lots of casual investors wanted
		in. The catch: an IPO only takes applications for a few days, and it was
		easy to miss the window. Brokers and finance sites had the data, but none
		of them sent a reliable heads-up.
	</p>
	<p>
		So one weekend in April 2021, I built ipoalerts: a small service that
		emailed subscribers about upcoming IPOs and the dates that mattered. It
		grew to over 200 subscribers, and for a while you could even reach it
		<a href="/blog/port-a-website-to-the-dark-web-in-under-2-minutes" data-umami-event="ipoalerts-tor">over Tor</a>.
	</p>
	<p>
		Then the numbers caught up with it. Fewer than 5% of people opened an
		alert on the day it was sent, which was the only day it was useful, and
		running it cost more than it was worth. Moving the alerts to WhatsApp
		might have reached people in time, but the WhatsApp Business API was far
		too expensive back then. I shut the emails down later that year.
	</p>

	<h2>From alerts to an API</h2>

	<p>
		The API and docs behind those emails never went offline, though. In 2024,
		developers started writing in to ask for IPO data, so I turned ipoalerts
		into a proper API, with API keys, rate limits, caching and a self-serve
		way to get started.
	</p>
	<p>
		It
		<a href="https://ipoalerts.in/blog/announcing-ipoalerts/" data-umami-event="ipoalerts-announcement">relaunched</a>
		in September 2024. A dashboard for keys and usage followed that December,
		and grey market premium trends joined the IPO data in August 2026.
	</p>

	<h2>What it does</h2>

	<ul>
		<li>
			<strong>IPO Data API.</strong> Every IPO on NSE and BSE since 2012, with
			30+ fields per issue: every date from bidding to listing, price band, lot
			size, subscription numbers, listing gains, and a short read on the
			business, its strengths and its risks. Filter by status, type, exchange
			or year.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>GMP Trends API.</strong> Grey market premium as a time series,
			down to 5-minute intervals, combined from several public sources and
			summarised as the mean, median, min, max or mode.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>A dashboard.</strong> API keys, usage and your plan, all in one
			place.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Quickstarts in 12 languages.</strong> From JavaScript and Python
			to Swift and Kotlin, so it takes a couple of minutes to wire up.
		</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>How it works</h2>

	<p>
		ipoalerts doesn't have a private line into the exchanges. It collects
		publicly available data (exchange announcements, registrars, brokers,
		issuer filings and GMP trackers), merges it into one clean record per IPO,
		and serves that over a REST API.
	</p>

	<pre
		class="diagram"
		role="img"
		aria-label="Exchanges and filings, registrars and brokers, and GMP trackers all feed into ipoalerts, which merges and refreshes every IPO and serves it to fintech apps and websites through the /ipos and /ipos/{id}/gmp endpoints."
	>{diagram}</pre>

	<p>Asking for the IPOs open right now looks like this:</p>

	<pre class="sample"><code>{sample}</code></pre>

	<p>
		Because it's aggregated rather than official, the data can lag by a few
		minutes. For anything that matters, check it against the exchange.
	</p>

	<h2>Using ipoalerts</h2>

	<p>
		There's a free tier with 25 requests a day for the IPOs that are open
		right now. Paid plans start at ₹499 a month and add the full history back
		to 2012, advanced filters and higher limits, with GMP data available as an
		add-on.
	</p>
	<p>
		Sign up at <a href="https://ipoalerts.in/" data-umami-event="ipoalerts-site">ipoalerts.in</a>,
		grab a key from the dashboard, and the
		<a href="https://ipoalerts.in/docs" data-umami-event="ipoalerts-docs">docs</a>
		take it from there. Questions, bugs and feature requests go to
		<a href="mailto:support@ipoalerts.in">support@ipoalerts.in</a>.
	</p>
</ProjectLayout>

<style>
	.intro {
		margin: 2rem 0;
	}

	p,
	li {
		font-size:   1.05rem;
		line-height: 1.7;
	}

	li + li {
		margin-top: 0.5rem;
	}

	h2 {
		margin-top: 2.5rem;
	}

	/* Scales down on small screens so all 32 columns fit, no scrolling. */
	.diagram {
		margin:           1.5rem 0;
		padding:          1rem 0.75rem;
		background-color: var(--code-bg);
		border-radius:    4px;
		font-size:        min(0.8rem, 2.9vw);
		line-height:      1.35;
	}

	/* Long lines scroll inside the box rather than widening the page. */
	.sample {
		margin:           1.5rem 0;
		padding:          1rem 0.75rem;
		overflow-x:       auto;
		background-color: var(--code-bg);
		border-radius:    4px;
		font-size:        0.8rem;
		line-height:      1.45;
	}
</style>
